}{y}^{′}(x) & =({x}^{2})^{′}=2x, \\\\ {y}^{″}(x) & =(2x)^{′}=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the equation, we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}(2)-2x(2x)=-2x.\\,\\,\\times \n$$\n\nSo, ${y}_{p}(x)={x}^{2}$ $\\text{isn't}$ a particular solution of the differential equation.\n\nWe are told that the complementary solution of our equation is ${y}_{c}(x)=A{x}^{3}+B.$ Therefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(x) & ={y}_{c}(x)+{y}_{p}(x) \\\\  & =A{x}^{3}+B+x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $A\\text{ and }B$ are arbitrary constants." 13194139533471 17592186045585 true] [17592186397366 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397367 13194139533471 17592186045585 true] [17592186397366 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397368 13194139533471 17592186045585 true] [17592186397366 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045494 13194139533471 17592186045585 true] [17592186397366 1077 "field-1" 13194139533471 17592186045585 true] [17592186397366 1079 #edb/ref 17592186397368 13194139533471 17592186045585 true] [17592186397366 1080 #uuid "bcb669d8-5345-5c4e-b897-7495dd431c78" 13194139533471 17592186045585 true] [17592186397367 1081 "isn't" 13194139533471 17592186045585 true] [17592186397367 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533471 17592186045585 true] [17592186397367 1084 #uuid "de93b087-2c87-54a2-8ce4-861cedbe5c5a" 13194139533471 17592186045585 true] [17592186397368 1081 "is" 13194139533471 17592186045585 true] [17592186397368 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533471 17592186045585 true] [17592186397368 1084 #uuid "38b22569-4620-5db6-9463-291c3a777e54" 13194139533471 17592186045585 true] [17592186397369 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397370 13194139533471 17592186045585 true] [17592186397369 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397371 13194139533471 17592186045585 true] [17592186397369 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397372 13194139533471 17592186045585 true] [17592186397369 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397373 13194139533471 17592186045585 true] [17592186397369 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045494 13194139533471 17592186045585 true] [17592186397369 1077 "field